--!strict
-- PLD-02 (Mech2) mesh table + templates. The 61 meshes in
-- assets/meshes/mech2 (legs / head / arms / torso, one MeshPart per colour
-- per rigid segment; the finger segments are not used, the HandMerged hands
-- are; the torso skirt plates are split into tasset_R / tasset_L, hinged
-- over each hip so they swing with the thigh) were uploaded by the owner
-- (asset_ids.json). Templates live in
-- ReplicatedStorage.Mech2Meshes (one MeshPart per name): Mech2Meshes.ensure()
-- loads any missing ones with InsertService:LoadAsset (edit mode via the
-- plugin, or the server at start-up), so the mech builds even when the
-- edit-mode templates were never saved.
--
-- Each entry: the bone it is welded to (Mech2Builder), the mesh bounding-box
-- centre in that bone's frame, its size and palette role. Generated by
-- assets/meshes/mech2/make_luau.py from the uploaded OBJs (bone frames = the
-- source folders' frames: torso segment pivots / sockets, head origin (neck
-- base), arm frames (shoulder ball, hanging), leg segment pivots).
--
-- Studio's importer turned every mesh 180 deg about Y (x -> -x, z -> -z;
-- checked vertex by vertex with EditableMesh against Leg_R_Thigh_White.obj),
-- like the BRZ-01 meshes, so templates are placed with ImportRotation.

local InsertService = game:GetService("InsertService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Mech2Meshes = {}

Mech2Meshes.FolderName = "Mech2Meshes"
Mech2Meshes.ImportRotation = CFrame.Angles(0, math.pi, 0)

export type Entry = { bone: string, role: string, offset: Vector3, size: Vector3, model: number, mesh: number }

